    "result_text": "All tests pass (the project has a single test class with the 3 postcode tests). Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Changes\n\nThe spec required an optional 4-digit `postcode` on owners, stored and returned when given, and rejected with 400 when out of range for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), while cities with no known region accept any 4-digit postcode.\n\nI kept structural impact low by adding behaviour as small, cohesive units and **not editing any existing method**:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property (`^[0-9]{4}$`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` inherits `OwnerFields`, it flows to both the request DTO and the response DTO, and MapStruct auto-maps it by name \u2014 **no mapper change needed**.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `postcode` column plus a trivial getter/setter (two new CC-1 methods; no existing method touched).\n\n3. **`rest/advice/OwnerPostcodeValidationAdvice.java`** (new) \u2014 a self-contained `RequestBodyAdvice`, mirroring the existing `OwnerCityCapacityAdvice`/`OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice` pattern. It rejects with 400 only when a postcode is present *and* the city maps to a known region *and* the value is out of range. It has `WMC_other = 0` (fresh class), so it adds almost nothing to the cost. Malformed (non-4-digit) postcodes are deliberately left to `@Pattern` bean validation, which also yields 400 \u2014 avoiding a `NumberFormatException`/500 since the advice runs before validation.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** and **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `postcode` column and a trailing `NULL` to the positional seed inserts (required for the test DB to load). I followed the repo's existing pattern of only keeping the hsqldb schema in sync \u2014 the h2/postgres/mysql schemas already omit the newer columns and rely on `ddl-auto`, so touching them would add cost without benefit.\n\nThe provided acceptance tests (`coreStoresValidPostcode`, `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`, `errorRejectsMalformedPostcode`) and the full build are green.",
